course: dictionary
lesson: 8471
title: Saltwater and freshwater
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are made from two smaller words joined together. Saltwater is made from salt and water. It means water that has salt in it, like sea water.
explain: Use the context to check. «The saltwater crocodile is the largest living reptile, with big males over 6 metres long, and it can travel by sea between islands.» The sea is salt water, so saltwater tells you this crocodile lives in or comes from the sea.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. «Sea water» fits, so your meaning works. Saltwater can also describe a thing, as in saltwater fish, meaning fish that live in the sea and not in fresh water.
fact: Saltwater means water that has salt in it, like sea water.
fact: Freshwater means water with little or no salt, like rivers and most lakes.
fact: Most of Earth's water is saltwater, found in the oceans.
fact: «Saltwater crocodiles» live in both salt and fresh water, and they can swim far out to sea.
fact: In a science test, an egg floats in salt water, so salt changes how things float.
exercise: Saltwater is water that has salt in it, like sea water. Which one is saltwater? | *The ocean | A river after rain | A pond in the park | A glass of tap water
exercise: In «saltwater fish», what kind of fish is it? | Fish that live in a pond | Frozen fish | Fish that are made of salt | *Fish that live in the sea, not in fresh water
exercise: Saltwater is made from two smaller words. Which two? | salty and waterfall | sat and water | *salt and water | sea and water
test: In the experiment, the egg floats in saltwater. Which kind of water is it? | *Water with salt in it | Boiled water | Fresh water | Warm water
test: «Saltwater crocodiles live in both salt and fresh water.» What does this tell you? | They only live on land | They cannot swim | They only live in ponds | *They can live in salt water and in fresh water
exam: Most of Earth's water is saltwater. Where is most of it found? | In clouds only | *In the oceans | In bottles | In ponds
